 us to scale efficiently while our team focuses on higher-complexity work.\n\nTerri Moran\n\nChief Underwriting Officer, Paul Hanson Partners\n\n> They know insurance, they know the business. We don’t have to question them.\n\nGeorge Karosa\n\nDirector of Operations, AssuredPartners\n\n## We meet you where you are\n\nImage\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAutomation Today: Publication & Newsletter: Clearing the Path for Human Expertise: How Tokio Marine HCC is Automating Underwriting, Not the Underwriter (https://automationtoday.net/featuredarticles/clearing-the-path-for-human-expertise-how-tokio-marine-hcc-is-automating-underwriting-not-the-underwriter/)\nciteturn1search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: 3 days ago;   * October 3, 2026 ... The approach is now being tested in specialty insurance underwriting, where Tokio Marine HCC is preparing to put an agentic AI-based submissions-prioritization system into production. ... They had to research the applicant, examine the material and compare it all against underwriting requirements before determining whether a risk was one the company wanted to consider. ... The underwriter, freed from more time-consuming work, can now review the prioritized submissions and use their specialized knowledge to decide whether to accept the business or not based on the merits of the case.\n  * October 3, 2026\n\n#### NEWS FOR THE AI-POWERED INTELLIGENT AUTOMATION ECOSYSTEM\n\nImage: Clearing the Path for Human Expertise: How Tokio Marine HCC is Automating Underwriting, Not the Underwriter\n\nUnderwriting is the beating heart of the insurance business. But for a company that has evolved into one of the largest specialty insurers in the world, how it assesses risk across more than 100 products makes that process even more complex. So, while Tokio Marine HCC is committed to optimizing underwriting through intelligent automation, Tamer Assaad would rather they leave the human underwriters right where they are.\n\nAssaad, the company’s vice president of digital transformation and financial systems, oversees an intelligent automation team that grew out of a traditional RPA Center of Excellence. This evolution, he says, reflects a broader shift in what automation can achieve and how it gets there.\n\nAgentic AI, Assaad tells Automation Today, has changed the paradigm guiding automation. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - 40447DXB9_final_prospectus_5Y_ACIBN_MQVTUSLE_013026(1756758778.2) (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/83246/000110465926009866/tm264785d61_424b2.pdf)\nciteturn1search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; <tr><td>September 1, 2026</td><td></td><td>September 4, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>September 30, 2026</td><td></td><td>October 5, 2026</td></tr>\nObservation Dates and Coupon Payment Dates:\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr><th>Observation Dates</th><th></th><th>Coupon Payment Dates</th></tr>\n<tr><td>February 27, 2026</td><td></td><td>March 4, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>March 31, 2026</td><td></td><td>April 6, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>April 29, 2026</td><td></td><td>May 4, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>June 1, 2026</td><td></td><td>June 4, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>June 30, 2026</td><td></td><td>July 6, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>July 30, 2026</td><td></td><td>August 4, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>September 1, 2026</td><td></td><td>September 4, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>September 30, 2026</td><td></td><td>October 5, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>October 30, 2026</td><td></td><td>November 4, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>December 1, 2026</td><td></td><td>December 4, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>December 29, 2026</td><td></td><td>January 4, 2027</td></tr>\n<tr><td>February 1, 2027 *</td><td></td><td>February 4, 2027 **</td></tr>\n<tr><td>March 1, 2027 *</td><td></td><td>March 4, 2027 **</td></tr>\n<tr><td>March 31, 2027 *</td><td></td><td>April 5, 2027 **</td></tr>\n<tr><td>April 29, 2027 *</td>